# Local workspace configuration.
#
# Harness permissions, model routing, and resolver settings depend on the
# developer's machine. Init still creates and hash-tracks this file so re-runs
# can preserve local edits and report template conflicts.
config/config.yaml

# Code review gate artifacts.
#
# The report-only review gate writes a recorded base commit and review.xml into
# the plan it is reviewing. A failed review may also leave reviewer-output.txt
# for diagnosis. These files are machine-generated output for one execution.
#
# Ignoring it also keeps the gate from reviewing itself. The reviewed diff runs
# from the recorded base against the working tree, and untracked files are in
# scope. The gate synthesizes an add-diff for each one. These rules keep its own
# output out because the gate enumerates untracked paths with
# `git ls-files --others --exclude-standard`.
#
# Both locations are listed because a completed plan directory is moved from
# plans/ to archive/ wholesale, carrying its review/ directory with it.
plans/*/review/
archive/*/review/

# Dispatch-availability cache.
#
# The dispatch target selector probes external harnesses and caches each
# outcome here, with a lifetime measured in minutes. It is machine-generated,
# host-specific, and never meaningful to another checkout. The directory is
# created on demand by the first probe, so it can appear in a workspace long
# after init ran — which is why it is covered from here rather than by an
# ignore file shipped inside it.
runtime/
